# React + TypeScript

## Components

- Use functional components and hooks
- Name components in PascalCase; match the file name (`Button.tsx` → `Button`)
- Props: use `interface` or `type`; avoid `any`

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
interface ButtonProps {
  label: string;
  onClick: () => void;
}

export function Button({ label, onClick }: ButtonProps) {
  return <button type="button" onClick={onClick}>{label}</button>;
}
```

## Hooks

- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks (`use*` prefix)
- Keep dependency arrays for `useEffect`, `useMemo`, and `useCallback` complete and accurate

## TypeScript

- Prefer `interface` for object props; use `type` for unions and intersections
- Export types from the same module when used elsewhere
- Handle errors with proper types; do not use empty `catch` blocks

## Style

- One component per file (except small barrel `index.ts` files)
- Colocate tests and stories next to the component when present (`Button.test.tsx`)

## Avoid

- Class components (unless required)
- `default export` for main components if the project consistently uses named exports
- New inline objects/functions in JSX when they cause unnecessary re-renders — memoize or extract them
